#: page-detail.php:112
msgid "1. Opportunity overview"
msgstr ""

#: page-detail.php:113
msgid ""
"Lacer is seeking to identify and develop innovative solutions that address the\n"
"                        root cause of gingivitis by actively restoring oral microbiome balance (eubiosis), moving beyond\n"
"                        traditional 'kill bacteria' strategies."
msgstr ""

#: page-detail.php:122
msgid "Desired outcome"
msgstr ""

#: page-detail.php:125
msgid ""
"A proven ability to shift the\n"
"                                    oral microbiome composition from a dysbiotic to a eubiotic state."
msgstr ""

#: page-detail.php:127
msgid ""
"A targeted reduction of key\n"
"                                    pathogenic species associated with gingivitis."
msgstr ""

#: page-detail.php:129
msgid ""
"The simultaneous increase or\n"
"                                    preservation of beneficial commensal bacteria to deliver more sustainable clinical\n"
"                                    outcomes."
msgstr ""

#: page-detail.php:138
msgid "2. What we are looking for"
msgstr ""

#: page-detail.php:139
msgid ""
"While current gingivitis treatments primarily rely on broad bacterial reduction\n"
"                        (antiseptics) or symptom control (anti-inflammatories), emerging science indicates that\n"
"                        long-term oral health depends on precise microbiome modulation. Lacer aims to establish\n"
"                        leadership in microbiome-based oral care by integrating this science into next-generation\n"
"                        products, enabling new differentiated claims such as reversing early-stage gingivitis by\n"
"                        targeting underlying imbalances."
msgstr ""

#: page-detail.php:149
msgid "3. Must-have requirements"
msgstr ""

#: page-detail.php:153
msgid "Maturity"
msgstr ""

#: page-detail.php:154
msgid "Technology Readiness Level (TRL) of &gt; 5."
msgstr ""

#: page-detail.php:158
msgid "Microbiome Modulation"
msgstr ""

#: page-detail.php:159
msgid "Antimicrobial activity in multispecies oral biofilm models"
msgstr ""

#: page-detail.php:163
msgid "Validation Method"
msgstr ""

#: page-detail.php:164
msgid "16S rRNA gene sequencing."
msgstr ""

#: page-detail.php:168
msgid "Biological Relevance"
msgstr ""

#: page-detail.php:169
msgid "Cosmetic, medical device, or food supplement"
msgstr ""

#: page-detail.php:173
msgid "Regulatory Framework"
msgstr ""

#: page-detail.php:174
msgid "Spain, the European Union, &amp; Latin America"
msgstr ""

#: page-detail.php:181
msgid "4. Nice to have"
msgstr ""

#: page-detail.php:188
msgid ""
"We are looking for technologies at least capable of demonstrating\n"
"                            efficacy in patients with Grade 2 gingivitis, ideally showing measurable improvements."
msgstr ""

#: page-detail.php:195
msgid "5. Related Keywords"
